# Constitution

Short always-on norms. Details live in `playwright-conventions.mdc`, `qa-orchestration.mdc`, and `.cursor/skills`.

## MUST

| Practice | Rule |
|----------|------|
| Locators | Role-based (`getByRole` first); POM only — no inline locators in specs |
| Waiting | Web-first assertions (`expect(locator).…`); never boolean snapshots |
| Auth | `storageState` + setup project; no per-test login UI |
| Data | Unique names (Faker/timestamp); delete what you create |
| Tags | Exactly one of `@smoke`, `@sanity`, `@regression`, `@api`, `@e2e`, `@destructive` per `test()` — not on `describe` |

## SHOULD

| Practice | Rule |
|----------|------|
| Factories | Faker (or shared helpers) for variable test input |
| Enums | Named constants for repeated UI/API strings |
| POM docs | JSDoc on public page actions |

## WON'T

| Anti-pattern | Why |
|--------------|-----|
| XPath / fragile CSS | Breaks on DOM drift |
| `waitForTimeout` | Flaky, masks real readiness |
| Hardcoded secrets | Use env / CI secrets |
| `any` | Type real shapes |
| Weakened assertions | Don't greenwash failures |
| Heal a real app bug | File bug; patch locators only after drift triage |
| Tags on `describe` | One tag per test |

## Agent governance

Behavioral norms for the agent — not enforced by hooks. Apply on every non-trivial task (multi-file edits, new tests, orchestration, infra, or anything where wrong assumptions are costly). Trivial one-line fixes and pure Q&A may skip the Proposal block.

### Audit-then-edit

1. **Audit** — Read relevant files, search the repo, use MCP/tools, or ask the human until facts are grounded (paths, APIs, env vars, copy, Jira keys).
2. **Propose** — Emit a **Proposal** block (below) before the first edit.
3. **Edit** — Change only what the approved scope covers; re-audit if new unknowns appear.

### Proposal block (required before edits)

```markdown
## Proposal

**Scope:** <what will change, files/areas touched>
**Confidence:** <1–10>
**Rationale:** <why this approach matches repo conventions and the request>
**Unknowns:** <open questions, or "none">
```

### Confidence gate

| Confidence | Action |
|------------|--------|
| **&lt; 5** | Do **not** edit. Ask for the missing input or explore further. |
| **5–7** | List **Unknowns** explicitly; proceed only after **human approval** of scope and risks. |
| **≥ 8** | Proceed with audit-then-edit; still document Unknowns if any remain. |

Re-score confidence after audit if new evidence lowers it — a gate failure overrides momentum.

### No fabrication

Never invent a **path**, **enum**, **env var**, **credential**, or **user-facing message** (UI copy, error text, ticket title). If not verified in repo, live app, Jira, or env docs — **ask** or **explore** (grep, read, MCP crawl) first.

